the edgy kids who make up the DC  extended universe is Suicide Squad are a  far cry from the comics original team of  straight-laced heroes while the original  crew simply strove for the benefit of  mankind the modern squads interests are  generally a bit more unpredictable which  is not to say that the Suicide Squad  hasn't always been filled with a fair  dose of crazy here's a look at the  squad's weird history origins secret  origins number 14 reveals that squadron  s was where the army put all of their  crazier soldiers who would either get  the job done or kill each other the crew  took the name Suicide Squad not because  they were willing to die but because  most soldiers would rather kill  themselves than join squadron s the  dysfunctional team is headed up by Rick  Flagg senior and they're called into  action to fight super threats after the  Justice Society of America temporarily  quits much later Rick Flagg jr. takes  over his dad's legacy after Rick's  senior kills himself fighting the war  wheel while still in mourning for his  deceased wife flag Jr's team first  appears in 1959 s the brave in the bold  number 25 colonel rick flagg jr. karen  grace jess bright and dr. hugh evans are  all the last living members of their  respective teams all willing to die to  save the world and uplift their lost  friends legacies they're basically a  crew powered by pure survivor's guilt  even in their first appearance fighting  a giant red hot dinosaur the squad makes  it clear that their event suicidal but  for all the right reasons  after about fifty issues bright and  Evans are swallowed up in an icy  crevasse while battling a Yeti the team  disbands and the two are assumed dead  for years  bright however survives by pulling a  page right out of Star Wars and digging  himself into the warm Yeti carcass the  Chinese government eventually finds him  removes his busted body parts and uses  their own super soldier program  rescue him so they can use a scientific  genius right now angry and insane goes  on to create a terrorist supervillain  team called the jihad who flag the squad  for decades after the team disband and  reforms The Suicide Squad again becomes  the repository for the unwanted but  instead of just really bad soldiers  Flagg jr. has to manage semi reformed  supervillains the squad is a great place  for DC Comics to put their stranger  villains digging up obscure comic  history along the way Harley Quinn dr.  Harleen Quinzel entered DC Comics as an  under qualified Arkham Asylum  psychiatrist who falls under the Joker's  grosse spell she became a fan favorite  villain pretty quickly but most readers  seemed to just ignore the fact that the  Joker has tried to kill Harley more  times than her enemies ever have despite  regular abuse her infatuation with the  Clown Prince of Crime continued for  about two decades until her writers  realized that depicting an abusive  relationship as endearing wasn't really  responsible in Harley Quinn number 25  she beat the Joker to a pulp in his own  prison cell completely biting off his  lower lip in the process making it very  hard for him to smile that winning grin  Deadshot Floyd Lawton is an assassin  with a heart of gold and a cyborg eye  who embodied the spirit of the Suicide  Squad better than any other member he  has no wish to live refuses to commit  suicide and wants to die in an  honourable way Deadshot strangest  adventure is set off by an airport  employee who steals his costume from his  luggage and goes around killing innocent  people forcing the real Deadshot to well  shoot him dead shooting a guy dressed as  himself messes up Deadshot for a while  until he's possessed by a demon tries to  blow up some kids in an elementary  school and then tries to kill the Pope  which is probably the worst thing a  comic character has ever attempted  El Diablo the name el Diablo has  generally applied to heroic characters  in DC's history but the modern el Diablo  is first seen accidentally killing the  entire innocent family of a rival gang  member he seeks redemption by joining  the squad and frequently voices his  objections to any senseless killing  during his very first outing with the  squad the team has to contain a stadium  full of humans infected with a robo  virus that kinda turns them into zombies  when El Diablo and Deadshot are attacked  by a pregnant woman bot Diablo is the  one who protects her from being killed  she mutates into a crazy Java blob king  shark bites her head off and the team  delivers a healthy baby by slicing it  out of the monster's belly the whole  thing sets off a rivalry between Diablo  and Deadshot katana  while most of these Suicide Squad  members are part of Batman's rogues  gallery katana actually worked alongside  Batman in his team The Outsiders she  still doesn't completely fit into the  superhero model as she wields a sword  that steals Souls and heroes generally  like to leave Souls in the bodies they  came from katana sword has a pretty  special relationship with death so the  heroine was able to help stop the Black  Lantern zombies plans when they invaded  earth during the epic DC Comics events  blackest night so while carrying around  a sword full of tortured souls is a  pretty sucky superpower to have it's not  altogether useless corpse whispering is  a pretty profitable back-up plan if the  whole hero thing doesn't work out just  ask John Edward and chant hrus if you go  to a party at a creepy Castle don't  wander around or else you run the risk  of being possessed by an ancient space  witch that's just common sense  unfortunately June moon didn't get the  memo now she plays host to a powerful  evil that she can only sometimes control  causing her to unpredictably split  between hero and villain after a while  the forces that gave enchantress her  powers went rotten so she turned crazy  and attacked Supergirl earning her new  villain status enchantress has been  separated from and reunited with the  Dark Soul that fuels her a few times  leaving her catatonic or tucked safely  away in an asylum so she's kind of  dammed either way all of this makes her  a pretty good candidate for the Suicide  Squad Captain Boomerang remember the  time you brought your teddy bear to  school and everyone laughed at you so  you decided to go home and become a  teddy bear themed super villain that's  pretty much the origin story of Captain  Boomerang except with boomerangs digger  Harkness is probably one of the worst  human alive in the DC Universe  he's outwardly racist he's cowardly and  he went on a pie-throwing rampage  against his teammates that lasted a year  and a half eventually everyone got so  tired of them that he was dropped on a  deserted island until the squad needed  him again  when he was picked up he'd grown a  wicked beard and was trying to build a  giant boomerang to fly himself home  because not only is he a jerk but he's  pretty stupid too his first mission back  dressing up like Batman to distract some  bad guys because captain boomerangs best  power is being a human target Killer  Croc  Waylon Jones has more origin stories  than teeth and that's a lot for a  man-eating crocodile person whether his  condition was caused by a skin disease a  gypsy curse bad steroids or genetic  experiments gone wrong croc is now a guy  who is super strong super dumb and  hungry for living meat when Batman came  nosing around he was getting closer  closer  I threw rock that in crock actually has  a special relationship with DC weirdo  Swamp Thing  at one point Swamp Thing [ __ ] crock  into breaking out of Arkham causing  Batman to pursue him all the way to  Louisiana after a battle through the  muck Swamp Thing subdues Batman with a  puff of psychotropic pollen convincing  Batman to let the animalistic croc  finally find peace and solitude in the  swamps at least for a little while  Slipknot years before the metal band of  the same name made its debut Slipknot  was a forgettable villain the bad guy is  first seen attacking DC hero firestorm  using a gimmick even worse than Captain  Boomerang boomerangs ropes sure they're  durable ropes but they're still ropes  and even though DC Comics already had  its ultimate durable rope and Wonder  Woman's lasso of truth they still needed  more ropes and that Slipknot Slipknot's  worst moment comes at the hands of  boomerang in order to keep the Suicide  Squad in check each member is fitted  with exclusive wristbands that can't go  beyond a certain range or they'll  explode  boomerang isn't keen on using himself to  test whether or not these explosive  devices are real so he convinces  Slipknot that they're fake Slipknot  takes the first opportunity to escape  only to have his arm blown off by a very  real explosive wrist bomb which makes it  pretty hard to tie Slipknot for a while  thanks for watching subscribe to our  YouTube channel to watch more videos  like the one you just saw and leave us a  comment to let us know your favorite  Suicide Squad member
 

